<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hasan Agha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1545">1545</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hasan Agha was a Sardinian-born convert and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eunuch">eunuch</a> who rose in the service of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hayreddin-barbarossa">Hayreddin Barbarossa</a> and governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a> as his deputy from 1533. In October 1541 he led the defence of the city against the great expedition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a>, whose fleet was wrecked by a storm and whose army was forced to re-embark. He remained in charge of Algiers until shortly before his death in 1545.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hasan-agha.jpg" alt="Hasan Agha" width="320" height="266" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anonymous 1555 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Siege_of_Algiers_1541.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
